The monolithic local normal-form replay hit the stated 600-second cap and produced no certificate. I’m switching to the staged proof the checkpoints naturally support: at each band, retain the earlier certified generators, add exactly the Jacobian-rank increment, and reduce only that band’s dependent rows. This decomposes the same localized-generation claim into 19 small exact checks; later bands with full rank increments require no reduction at all.
